**About Us:**



Network Rail Consulting (NRC) is the international consultancy arm of Network Rail, the owner and operator of Britain’s railway. Since 2013, we’ve delivered over 200 consultancy contracts across Australia, the Middle East, and North America, supporting government agencies, public and private organisations, and passenger and freight operators.



Our reputation is built on consistently high levels of client satisfaction and technical expertise. We are driven by our core values: **Agile, Always Safe, Care About People, Collaborative, Impartial and Passionate.**


**We offer a competitive and flexible employee experience, including:**


* Highly competitive market rate salaries;
* Generous annual leave \- 25 days per year, plus the option to buy or sell leave;
* Above award Parental Leave program;
* Life Insurance \& Total Permanent Disability cover;
* Novated car leasing arrangements;
* Career development pathways;
* Learning \& development programs;
* Rewards Gateway employee discounts; and
* Flexible working arrangements.


**About the role:**



We are seeking a highly motivated Graduate Engineer with a passion for building a career in the rail industry to join our growing Sydney team.



As part of our structured three\-year Graduate Development Program, you will gain hands\-on experience across a diverse range of rail projects, rotate through different disciplines every six months, and undertake a fully supported six\-week UK immersion placement with our parent company, Network Rail. This unique opportunity provides international exposure, access to industry\-leading rail expertise, and the chance to build a global professional network.



You will hold a degree in Mechanical, Mechatronic, Electrical, Civil or Systems Engineering and have strong communication, report\-writing and teamwork skills, along with a commitment to continuous learning and development.



Working alongside experienced consultants and technical specialists, you will develop the technical, commercial and consultancy skills needed to establish a successful long\-term career in the rail sector.



Throughout the program, you will gain exposure to:


* Advisory \& Strategic Planning;
* Railway Operations;
* Systems Engineering \& Integration;
* Asset Management \& Maintenance; and
* Project \& Program Management.


You will contribute to a broad range of activities, including research and analytical project work, developing technical requirements, and supporting the preparation of bids and proposals.


**Our graduate program also includes:**


* Membership to Engineers Australia (the national body for Engineers with over 140,000 members);
* Enrolment on the industry recognised development program with Engineers Australia;
* Professional networking opportunities with rail industry professionals;
* Internal and external learning and development training courses;
* Support and access to peers and mentors; and
* Participation in the 'Go Global Grads Working Group’.


**About you**


* You will need to be an Australian citizen;
* Recently completed, or be in your final year of a degree in Mechanical, Mechatronic, Electrical, Civil or Systems Engineering;
* Strong interest in building a career in rail consulting;
* Able to manage multiple tasks, responsibilities and deadlines;
* Reliable, committed and professional in the workplace;
* Motivated by personal and professional development;
* Strong written and verbal communication skills;
* Proven report‑writing capability; and
* Results‑focused with strong attention to detail.


As part of the recruitment process, shortlisted candidates may be asked to provide a copy of their academic transcript(s) for assessment purposes.


**Sound interesting?**



To apply, please submit your resume along with a one\-page cover letter outlining your interest in joining an international rail consulting business.


**Pre\-Employment Checks**



The successful candidate will be required to undergo pre\-employment checks which include a national criminal history check, qualification check and references.


